          "name": "Flame of Justice",
          "kind": "passive",
          "description": "A gestalt's spirit of righteousness manifests in its hands as a mighty two-handed sword called the flame of justice.\nA gestalt can throw its flame of justice as a ranged weapon. If disarmed or thrown, the flame of justice vanishes after landing or dealing damage and reappears in the gestalt's hands again instantly.\nOn a critical hit, the fire damage from the flame of justice deals maximum damage 6 fire damage on the d6) before being doubled for the critical hit, and the target takes 1d10 persistent fire damage.",
