          "kind": "action",
          "description": "The anancus sweeps its long tusks back and forth, dealing 4d6 bludgeoning damage to all creatures in a 15-foot cone, who must make a check (reflex, dc:27, basic, options:area-effect,forced-movement,inflicts:prone) save.\nCritical Success The target is unaffected.\nSuccess The target takes half damage.\nFailure The target takes full damage and is knocked Prone.\nCritical Failure The target takes double damage, is knocked prone, and is pushed 5 feet away from the anancus.",
